from pathlib import Path
import json,hashlib,subprocess,shutil,statistics as st
r=Path('/home/truth/Code/my_kvraft');o=r/'benchmarks/results/block-cache-acceptance-20261119';rows=[json.loads(s) for s in (o/'runs.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()]
def hashes(p):return {str(x.relative_to(p)):hashlib.sha256(x.read_bytes()).hexdigest() for x in p.rglob('*') if x.is_file()}
assert hashes(r/'src/lsm')==hashes(o/'engine-snapshot')
formal=[v for v in rows if v['name'].startswith('formal')];assert len(formal)==234
assert all(v['usage']<=v['capacity'] for v in rows)
def cmd(*args):return subprocess.check_output(args,text=True,stderr=subprocess.STDOUT)
meta=dict(engine_hashes=hashes(o/'engine-snapshot'),fixture_hashes=hashes(o/'fixtures'),git_after=cmd('git','-C',str(r),'status','--short'),compiler=cmd('c++','--version'),uname=cmd('uname','-a'),cpu=cmd('lscpu'),filesystem=cmd('df','-T',str(o)),cmake_cache=(r/'build/block-cache-accept/CMakeCache.txt').read_text(),build_commands=cmd('ninja','-C',str(r/'build/block-cache-accept'),'-t','commands'),seed=20261115,key_bytes=16,value_bytes=128,logical_keys=8192,requests_per_pass=8192,repeats=3,diagnostics=False)
(o/'metadata.json').write_text(json.dumps(meta,indent=2))
shutil.copytree(r/'benchmarks/block_cache_acceptance',o/'tools',ignore=shutil.ignore_patterns('__pycache__'))
text=['Block cache acceptance: evidence and reproduction','', 'Correctness: 14/14 existing test targets rebuilt/passed. Existing cache tests cover file identity at equal offset, cached older/newer versions and tombstones, eviction/lifetime, oversized bypass and read failure on miss, cross-block snapshot versions. No engine correctness failure observed. All formal/mechanism traces checked outside timing. Engine snapshot SHA256 matches unchanged workspace. No Git commit/push; existing changes and historical results retained.','', 'Capacity: charge = raw block body size, not trailing CRC or object/index/LRU allocator overhead. 1-table histogram 327*4025 + 2737; 64-table histogram 320*4025 + 64*483. Both total 1318912 B. Full 1318912 B, small 164864 B (12.5%). Full covers all possible data blocks, so is a conservative upper bound for each particular trace. Usage of a trace may be smaller; measured Usage in formal.csv. Hot 8 adjacent latest-table records use 4025 B, fit small capacity.','', 'Matrix: Reader paths 1/64 tables x latest/oldest/missing/hot/uniform x 0/full/small; DB only 64 tables x oldest/hot/uniform x 0/full/small. Each case starts a new process and fresh cache. Fixed logical 8192 keys, 16B keys, 128B version-identified values; single version per key, even numeric keys interleaved among tables with overlapping ranges. Missing keys are odd and inside range. Legacy CRC trace mapping/seed reused for latest/oldest/missing. Uniform uses seeded replacement sampling; hot repeats 8 records. Same trace and files across capacities; hashes preserved.','', 'Prewarm: independent Readers with capacity 0 traverse and verify each physical table own keys, then close. Create round DB/Readers with own empty shared cache. Pass 0 fill, same trace pass 1 stable. No drop_caches, OS-warm and engine-cache-empty, not cold disk. Every workload gets its own cache, not shared across configurations. All opens/validation/output excluded from request timing. Input trace/expected results prebuilt. Result checks after each pass; DB/Readers close before serialization. Single foreground thread.','', 'Formal cache-bench has diagnostics OFF, no Get/Insert/pread wrappers. Constructor-only wrapper retains actual cache pointer, so Usage is measured also for DB without private-access hacks. It adds no per-request instrumentation. Reader gets shared cache and manifest fileNumber; distinct files always distinct stable IDs. Disabled capacity 0 still constructs/queries empty cache (current DB behavior), so baseline includes its empty-cache locks, not the separate null-cache Reader path.','', 'Mechanism program is separate: linker wrappers around BlockCache Get/Insert and pread. Get result counts true block-cache hits/misses; Insert attempt corresponds to actual successful ReadBlock plus DataBlockReader validation, counted charge+4 bytes. During trace only, so metadata initialization and prewarm excluded. Every miss=load, pread calls=2*loads checked; no short reads seen. Bloom rejection does not call cache and is excluded from lookup denominator; same-table cross-block requests each do independent cache lookup. Mechanism throughput is not formal performance.','']
text+=['Representative stable-phase medians (formal):']
for nt,path,kind in [(1,'reader','uniform'),(64,'reader','uniform'),(64,'reader','hot'),(64,'db','uniform')]:
 for label in ['disabled','full','small']:
  vs=[v for v in formal if (v['tables'],v['path'],v['kind'],v['capacity_label'],v['pass'])==(nt,path,kind,label,1)]
  text.append(str((nt,path,kind,label))+': '+str({k:st.median(v[k] for v in vs) for k in ['ops','usage','rss_kib','p99_us']})+' op/s range '+str([round(v['ops']) for v in vs]))
text+=['','Interpretation: full hits skip pread, CRC and DataBlockReader full construction validation; block-local lookup/decoding still occurs. Cache still sits behind table iteration, Bloom, index; 64-table old hits/misses retain those costs. Full uniform 64 mechanism pass1: 14846 block-cache lookups, all hits, zero loads. Small uniform: 1917/14846 hits (12.91%), 12929 loads, 50985837 bytes incl CRC; hot pass1 8192/8192 hits, zero loads, Usage 4025 B. Full first uniform pass has 383 misses; pass1 zero.','', 'Maintenance cost: stable small uniform net speedup about 9–13%, so no net regression seen in these cases, but this is NOT evidence of zero maintenance overhead. Misses still pay lookup/Insert/LRU/allocation and benefit from some hits. No isolated all-miss-vs-equivalent-work experiment in this matrix, cannot quantify pure maintenance time from net throughput. Frequent eviction inferred from loads/hits and bounded Usage; exact eviction counter not exposed, not fabricated. Full latest vs small ratios may cross by noise; no claim larger capacity must be faster.','', 'Memory: charge is ~1.26 MiB/full and ~0.157 MiB/small; formal VmHWM printed above is process high-water including prewarm, input/expected strings, result vectors and allocator retention, not incremental live cache bytes. Usage tracks charge only; memory budget is not strict RSS cap. Some tiny hot traces only occupy 4025 B even with full capacity; do not quote full configured capacity as allocated memory.','', 'Variability: use min/max ranges and all raw rounds. 8192 hot samples can take only a few ms and are sensitive to scheduling; reported 20x+ gains have mechanisms supporting removed loads but exact ratios and max latency are not stable worst-case guarantees. Missing queries that Bloom-reject most tables have fewer cache lookups; do not confuse improved miss latency with cache hit rate. Results are small warm single-thread workloads, not cold disk or concurrent scalability.','', 'Reproduce in fresh directories only:','cmake -S benchmarks/block_cache_acceptance -B NEW_BUILD -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DENGINE_ROOT=/absolute/path/engine-snapshot','cmake --build NEW_BUILD -j 4','NEW_BUILD/cache-bench NEW_FIXTURE_DIR 64 0 generate latest 1 UNUSED_PREFIX','NEW_BUILD/cache-bench FIXTURE_DIR 64 164864 reader uniform 8192 NEW_PREFIX','NEW_BUILD/cache-bench FIXTURE_DIR 64 1318912 db oldest 8192 NEW_PREFIX','NEW_BUILD/cache-mechanism FIXTURE_DIR 64 164864 reader uniform 8192 NEW_PREFIX','Run tool stages prepare (fixture/capacity/pilot), formal, mechanism after setting NEW result path. Formal uses 3 shuffled configuration rounds with seed 20261115+round. Do not rerun prepare.py/observe.py on existing outputs or already-patched tool. Exact commands per scenario are in runs.jsonl, source hashes/build commands in metadata.json; tools and engine snapshot saved.','', 'Changed files: added benchmarks/block_cache_acceptance/{CMakeLists.txt,bench.cc,prepare.py,observe.py,run.py,summarize.py,archive.py}; added result directory only. No existing engine/test/document file modified by this acceptance.']
(o/'evidence-and-reproduce.txt').write_text('\n'.join(text)+'\n')
print('\n'.join(text[text.index('Representative stable-phase medians (formal):'):text.index('Interpretation: full hits skip pread, CRC and DataBlockReader full construction validation; block-local lookup/decoding still occurs. Cache still sits behind table iteration, Bloom, index; 64-table old hits/misses retain those costs. Full uniform 64 mechanism pass1: 14846 block-cache lookups, all hits, zero loads. Small uniform: 1917/14846 hits (12.91%), 12929 loads, 50985837 bytes incl CRC; hot pass1 8192/8192 hits, zero loads, Usage 4025 B. Full first uniform pass has 383 misses; pass1 zero.')]))
